# Right to left
{.lead} An engine probe for dir: rtl. The whole layout flips through logical CSS, and the flow arrow mirrors to read in the writing direction. Content is kept English; only the direction is right-to-left.

```mdp:flow
First -> Second -> Third
```

## Lists flip too
- Markers move to the inline-start edge
- The quote border flips
- Tables align to the start

```mdp:stats
Direction: rtl
Layout source: logical CSS
Author positioning: none
```

> "Set dir: rtl and the engine positions everything; the author never does."
> {.cite} The spec

:::callout recommendation
Use lang plus dir for a real right-to-left document. The renderer flips lists, the quote border, table alignment, cards, and the flow arrow automatically.
:::
